WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.920
- Speaking of musical talent,

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.190
good singers and musicians
always impress me,

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:06.640
all right, but, you know
what also blows me away?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.998
It's the things I can't do.

00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:10.954
And we have a talented beatboxer, alright?

00:00:10.954 --> 00:00:14.290
It's a skill, it's a
skill that I don't have,

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.060
but I can definitely appreciate and I try

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.680
and do it when no one's around.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.180
(Laughter)

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.810
- (giggles) Or I'm drunk.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.490
And when you're drunk, you
think everything's great.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.190
There's a beatboxer
blowing up on social media

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.023
right now.

00:00:27.023 --> 00:00:29.231
He's so good, Will Smith has become a fan.

00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:32.460
Take a look at the video
that started it all.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.637
(beat boxing)

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:35.970
- I'm Spongebob.

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:39.446
(beat boxing)

00:00:39.446 --> 00:00:41.220
- Hi, Patrick.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.328
(beat boxing)

00:00:43.328 --> 00:00:48.328
- Hey, Spongebob. (beatboxing)

00:00:54.314 --> 00:00:55.880
- That's crazy, right?

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.200
I, okay. Well, that beat
boxer's name is Verbal Ace,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.550
and he's here today.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:02.597
Ya'll, stand up. (whooping)(clapping)

00:01:02.597 --> 00:01:05.302
[Kelly] Ya'll give it up for Verbal Ace.

00:01:05.302 --> 00:01:07.154
(clapping)

00:01:07.154 --> 00:01:08.200
[Kelly] I need..

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.960
- First of all, first of
all, I have a question.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.120
Like, as a vocalist.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.160
Does that hurt?

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.737
Verbal Ace - It used to. (laughter)

00:01:15.737 --> 00:01:18.250
[Kelly] Oh, you just trained
it, for that. I'm like

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.030
all like, breathing in and out. WHOO!

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.530
That's gotta be rough on the chords.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.870
- Yeah, that's the first
thing I actually had to learn

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.210
how to do is breathe,
beacause I used to just do

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.380
it until I'd run out of breath.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.480
Like (beatboxing) ugh.

00:01:31.002 --> 00:01:33.990
- My God, even that was cool, and that was

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:37.630
probably so simple for
you, but I'm blown away.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.597
Oh my gosh, okay, so you got
to beatbox with Will Smith.

00:01:40.597 --> 00:01:42.737
[Kelly] Like, how did that happen?

00:01:42.737 --> 00:01:44.230
[Verbal Ace] Uh, it all
started when I was a kid.

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:46.748
I would try to make sounds,
the same sounds I hear

00:01:46.748 --> 00:01:48.040
in video games.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.350
You know, play video
game (beatboxing) boom.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.860
Game over,[Kelly] Oh my gosh.
-And um, put stuff out on

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.386
social media, um, I have like
over 250M views throughout

00:01:58.386 --> 00:02:01.684
my whole social media. (clapping)

00:02:01.684 --> 00:02:02.517
[Kelly] What?

00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:06.350
- And this all started with
Will Smith's post, the one

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.890
at the airport clip on
his social media, and then

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:13.130
he posted another video the
same day saying he was obsessed.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.840
And um, I actually had the
opportunity to surprise him

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.400
on a tv show in London, and um,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.749
I didn't think he was going
to be there, cause it's

00:02:20.749 --> 00:02:21.582
Will Smith, come on.

00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:24.450
When I finally walked out
onstage, and I beatboxed

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:28.770
he screamed when he saw me.
And um, I had to, I had to

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.980
stay, I had to keep preforming
cause it's the first

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.520
time I'd met him in person.
So, in my head, I was still

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.673
doing the [Kelly] You're freaking out.

00:02:35.673 --> 00:02:38.371
- But you know, on camera,
I was like hey what's up.

00:02:38.371 --> 00:02:40.976
- You're like, its no big
deal. You're will smith,

00:02:40.976 --> 00:02:42.087
it's fine. Its fine.

00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:43.930
[Verbal Ace] Yeah, and it all
felt like a dream come true

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.484
like, I still couldn't
believe it happened.

00:02:46.484 --> 00:02:48.480
[Kelly] That's so amazing, man.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.488
(clapping)

00:02:49.488 --> 00:02:51.852
- That's so cool. Well, if
it's good enough for the

00:02:51.852 --> 00:02:54.276
Fresh Prince, let's see
what you got. Go ahead.

00:02:54.276 --> 00:02:56.693
(beatboxing)

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:16.367
(laughter)

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:18.617
(clapping)

00:03:27.779 --> 00:03:30.862
[Kelly] (sings)

00:03:30.862 --> 00:03:35.862
(clapping) (laughter)

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:39.280
- I just, I just, Verbal Ace,
I just gave away my secret.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.810
Any time I get lost in a
song, I do the Envogue (sings)

00:03:43.686 --> 00:03:46.688
- Like I know I am, but that sounds good.

00:03:46.688 --> 00:03:49.153
You're awesome man, you're fantastic.

